    title: "Linux 核心修復 s390/fpu 虛假陽性報告：修正 kmsan 檢測的內聯組語寫入大小判斷錯誤",
    summary: "本更新針對 Linux 核心在 s390/fpu 架構下，處理內聯組語（inline assembly）時，由 clang 生成的 kmsan 虛假陽性報告（false-positive report）進行修復。問題出在 `vstl` 內聯組語指令的寫入位元組數，其大小取決於運行時的 `index` 參數。由於 clang 錯誤地將寫入大小固定為 1 位元組，而實際情況下，當 `index` 大於 0 時，寫入的位元組數至少為 2 位元組。此修復透過手動呼叫 kmsan 函數，明確指示正確的寫入位元組數，從而消除這些誤報。此類問題屬於編譯器與核心元件層面的優化，主要影響開發者和資安研究人員的除錯流程。建議系統管理員應更新至包含此修復的 Linux 核心版本，以確保系統除錯報告的準確性。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "s390/fpu", "kmsan", "clang", "內聯組語", "Linux 核心修復"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel Fixes s390/fpu False Positive Report: Corrects Inline Assembly Write Size Determination in kmsan Detection",
    summary_en: "This update addresses a false-positive report generated by clang within the Linux kernel when handling inline assembly on the s390/fpu architecture. The issue resides in the write byte size of the `vstl` inline assembly instruction, which depends on the runtime `index` parameter. Because clang incorrectly fixed the write size to 1 byte, while in reality, when `index` is greater than 0, the write size is at least 2 bytes. This fix manually calls the kmsan function, explicitly specifying the correct write byte size, thereby eliminating these false reports. This type of issue relates to compiler and kernel component-level optimizations and primarily affects the debugging workflow of developers and security researchers. System administrators are advised to update to the Linux kernel version containing this fix to ensure the accuracy of system debugging reports.",
    tags_en: ["Linux Kernel", "s390/fpu", "kmsan", "clang", "inline assembly", "Linux Kernel Fix"],
    sources: [
      { name: "NVD CVE API", url: "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-68751", lang: "EN" }
    ]
