    title: "Linux 核心修補：修復 iavf 模組的 settime64 相關空指標解引用漏洞",
    summary: "本漏洞位於 Linux 核心的 iavf 模組，涉及 ptp_clock_settime() 函式。該函式錯誤地假設所有 ptp_clock 都已實作 settime64()，若未實作，可能導致空指標解引用（NULL dereference）的漏洞。修補措施是在 iavf 模組中，使用 -EOPNOTSUPP 方式為 settime64 進行存根（Stub），從而防止此類空指標解引用。此修補與 commit 329d050bbe63 的修補類似。由於原文未提供具體的受影響版本或CVSS評分，實務影響為核心模組的穩定性與安全性。建議系統管理員應升級至包含此修補的 Linux 核心版本，以確保系統的穩定運行。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "iavf", "ptp_clock_settime", "settime64", "空指標解引用", "Linux 核心修補"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel Patch: Fixes Null Pointer Dereference Vulnerability in iavf Module's settime64",
    summary_en: "This vulnerability resides in the iavf module of the Linux kernel and involves the ptp_clock_settime() function. The function incorrectly assumes that all ptp_clock implementations support settime64(). If they do not, it can lead to a Null Pointer Dereference vulnerability. The patch addresses this in the iavf module by using -EOPNOTSUPP to stub settime64(), thereby preventing this type of null pointer dereference. This fix is similar to the one in commit 329d050bbe63. Since the original text does not provide specific affected versions or CVSS scores, the practical impact relates to the stability and security of the core module. System administrators are advised to upgrade to a Linux kernel version containing this patch to ensure stable system operation.",
