    trackers: ["os", "security"],
    category: "Linux",
    title: "Linux 核心修補：修復 DRM vgem-fence 潛在死鎖，提升 IRQ 上下文安全性",
    summary: "本更新針對 Linux 核心中的 `drm/vgem-fence` 機制，修復了一個潛在的死鎖（deadlock）漏洞。該漏洞發生在處理 vgem fence 自動超時釋放的計時器時。在某些場景下，特別是在 IRQ（中斷）上下文運行時，如果沒有使用 `TIMER_IRQSAFE` 標誌，可能會導致不安全的鎖定操作，進而引發系統死鎖。開發者在 Intel DRM CI 測試環境中觀察到此問題。修補措施是確保在 `dma_fence_put()` 呼叫的最後一步，釋放計時器時使用 `timer_delete_sync()`，從而保證在 IRQ 上下文中的鎖定操作是安全的。此修補對於使用 DRM 相關功能的系統，特別是進行壓力測試或複雜圖形處理的環境，至關重要。建議系統管理員應升級至包含此修補的 Linux 核心版本以避免潛在的系統穩定性問題。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "drm", "vgem-fence", "dma_fence", "死鎖", "IRQ 上下文"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel Patch: Fixes Potential Deadlock in DRM vgem-fence, Enhances IRQ Context Safety",
    summary_en: "This update addresses the `drm/vgem-fence` mechanism within the Linux kernel, fixing a potential deadlock vulnerability. This vulnerability occurs when handling the timer for automatic timeout release of vgem fences. In certain scenarios, particularly when running in an IRQ (interrupt) context, if `TIMER_IRQSAFE` is not used, it can lead to unsafe locking operations, potentially causing system deadlocks. The issue was observed by developers in the Intel DRM CI testing environment. The fix ensures that `timer_delete_sync()` is used when releasing the timer in the final step of the `dma_fence_put()` call, thereby guaranteeing safe locking operations within the IRQ context. This patch is critical for systems utilizing DRM-related functionalities, especially in environments undergoing stress testing or complex graphics processing. System administrators are advised to upgrade to a Linux kernel version containing this patch to prevent potential system stability issues.",
    tags_en: ["Linux Kernel", "drm", "vgem-fence", "dma_fence", "deadlock", "IRQ Context"],
    sources: [
      { name: "NVD CVE API", url: "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-68757", lang: "EN" }
    ]
