    summary_en: "This security advisory reports that the Linux kernel has fixed a potential Use After Free (UAF) vulnerability in the hfs filesystem module. The vulnerability resides in the `hfs_correct_next_unused_CNID()` function. The root cause is that the code dereferences the `node` pointer on the same line after calling `hfs_bnode_put(node)` to release its reference count, leading to the use of an invalidated pointer. The fix involves adjusting the code sequence to ensure that the system retains a valid reference count when the `node` pointer is used. If left unpatched, this type of kernel-level vulnerability could potentially allow an attacker to execute malicious code or cause a system crash under specific conditions. System administrators using Linux kernels are advised to promptly update to the latest kernel version containing this fix to ensure system stability and security.",
