    title: "Linux 核心修補：解決 netpoll 設置失敗時的警告，避免未初始化工作佇列被取消",
    summary: "本修補針對 Linux 核心中的 netpoll 機制，解決了一個在設備設定失敗時發生的警告問題。當使用 IFF_DISABLE_NETPOLL 旗標的設備在執行 netconsole 設置時，如果初始化過程提前失敗，清理路徑會呼叫 `cancel_work_sync()`。然而，由於工作佇列（work queue）尚未初始化，此操作會觸發一個警告。修補的實質是將工作佇列的初始化函數 `INIT_WORK()` 提前到 `__netpoll_setup()` 函數的開頭。這樣可以確保無論設置過程在哪個點失敗，工作佇列都能被正確初始化，從而讓清理路徑能夠安全地取消它，避免系統發出不必要的警告。此修補屬於核心元件的穩定性提升，建議所有使用 Linux 核心的系統應更新到包含此修補的最新版本。",
    tags: ["Linux 核心", "netpoll", "work queue", "IFF_DISABLE_NETPOLL", "CVE-2025-68762", "核心穩定性"],
    title_en: "Linux Kernel Patch: Addresses Warning When netpoll Setup Fails, Preventing Cancellation of Uninitialized Workqueue",
    summary_en: "This patch targets the netpoll mechanism within the Linux kernel, resolving a warning issue that occurs when device setup fails. When a device using the IFF_DISABLE_NETPOLL flag executes netconsole setup, if the initialization process fails prematurely, the cleanup path calls `cancel_work_sync()`. However, because the workqueue has not been initialized, this operation triggers a warning. The patch essentially moves the workqueue initialization function `INIT_WORK()` to the beginning of the `__netpoll_setup()` function. This ensures that the workqueue is correctly initialized regardless of where the setup process fails, allowing the cleanup path to safely cancel it and prevent unnecessary system warnings. This patch improves core component stability, and all systems using the Linux kernel are advised to update to the latest version containing this fix.",
